Ephemeral-sandbox test limitation on this Windows host — 2026-11-24

Full suite (backend/.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q from backend/):
  5 failed, 1934 passed, 7 skipped in 1549.06s (see backend-pytest-full.log).

One of the five failures was a real regression and is fixed in T9:
  tests/dn/test_question_validator.py::test_every_source_sql_has_nonempty_primary_and_executes_repeatably
  It used the read-only shared runner for the new table-state DML fixtures.
  Fixed by routing table-state fixtures to a writable SandboxRunner in that
  test; rerun: 44 passed (test_question_validator.py + test_dml_grading.py).

The remaining four failures are environmental and pre-existing:
  tests/dn/test_ephemeral_sandbox.py::test_offline_container_limits_typed_execution_and_cleanup
  tests/dn/test_ephemeral_sandbox.py::test_failure_paths_cleanup_and_environment
  tests/dn/test_ephemeral_sandbox.py::test_statement_timeout_and_watchdog_remove_abandoned_lease
  tests/dn/test_ephemeral_sandbox.py::test_grading_admission_keeps_one_slot_across_datasets_and_releases_it

All four fail with "SandboxError: SQL executor returned an invalid response";
the local Docker CLI (C:\Users\kudot\docker-cli\docker\docker.EXE) returns an
empty stdout for `docker exec -i ...`/`docker run ...` in this host setup, so
the container JSON response cannot be read. This affects only the offline
ephemeral-container tests; the shared-sandbox suite (1934 tests) passes.

Verification that these four are not caused by T1–T9: the two protocol files
(backend/app/services/ephemeral_sandbox.py and backend/app/sandbox_job.py) were
temporarily restored to their pre-T7 versions from ac74ed1 and the same four
tests were rerun — identical 4 failed / 0 passed result (14.79s). Files were
then restored with `git checkout --`. All other sandbox grading paths,
including DML state capture (backend/tests/test_dml_grading.py), pass.

UPDATE (post-freeze, 2026-11-24): the four failures were subsequently fixed in
commit 27c3e14 (see bug-a-ephemeral-exec.md). The final full suite is green:
1945 passed, 7 skipped (backend-pytest-final.log). This log is retained as the
diagnostic evidence, not as a current failure claim.
